From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ned <ned@localhost>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:24:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] in: decode SGR wheel-right (Cb=67) instead of misreporting it

An SGR mouse report with Cb=67 is wheel-right. The decoder did not
recognize it, so it fell through and was misdecoded as a motion event
followed by a release -- losing the scroll entirely and synthesizing two
events that never happened.
---
 src/lib/in.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lib/in.c b/src/lib/in.c
index 864bb06..b7ffaf5 100644
--- a/src/lib/in.c
+++ b/src/lib/in.c
@@ -614,7 +614,7 @@ mouse_click(inputctx* ictx, unsigned release, char follow){
   }else{
     tni.evtype = NCTYPE_PRESS;
   }
-  if(mods % 4 == 3){
+  if(mods < 64 && mods % 4 == 3){ /* ned patch: wheel -- this sentinel only applies to the base button group */
     tni.id = NCKEY_MOTION;
     tni.evtype = NCTYPE_RELEASE;
   }else{
